{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5c077b75da2b64a399993a6f592f42d8ecfd16ca4f157e3f96d95ff951cf6d44","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"kunal12203/graperoot@e21c5b9cd3e3 snapshot 657d207f0df5b456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4783d23354b2723fa9c6c7d0d69d984b02074cb5c6fe7b0e69e6e25428251e39","slc_5034218196da616fb2aaef9406c3228c9ce3b6a4c7bfb5985763470e78655f0c"],"source_ids":["src_14a4201a4405575187012b548764bceb"],"text":"The README describes session memory: files that were read, edited, or queried are weighted higher in future turns, so context compounds across a session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6fc75c51afdd856b301b29649d70d932f64a94ad88b9389877bf7cb0129efba8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"kunal12203/graperoot@e21c5b9cd3e3 snapshot 657d207f0df5b456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f274a226d54b87083db13f5a05154611b06dbdfdd88ed1b25b0fabcf2ebc11e","slc_a233bd661fc7858473ab005b0fa0d557b205386d710cb6e0f5b32aed402d4e19","slc_de0729f2429f4aa5b22d1ff7dfff002f35c02b03c997dabc546ebff0a9730aa2"],"source_ids":["src_14a4201a4405575187012b548764bceb"],"text":"The README reports benchmarks over real-world codebases (7,700+ files) and 50+ prompts, claiming cost per prompt dropping from $0.49 to $0.27, average turns from 11.7 to 3.5, and quality scores from 76.6 to 86.6 out of 100, with full methodology at graperoot.dev/benchmarks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_87b802a21e8db6e32ae3c9f15dfb124050e28325f6b04a1bcc624f1d1c3f59de","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"kunal12203/graperoot@e21c5b9cd3e3 snapshot 657d207f0df5b456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b0bcb7cd5ea57eae3496d41c8e9b3a20f1c0a14651369e875f7ee53f1d0d2351","slc_d0060c183db5ff52d9a6738c6fcbaadc83da6478ce9efcd79b192362a42c4166"],"source_ids":["src_14a4201a4405575187012b548764bceb"],"text":"The tool targets developers using AI coding assistants on TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Go, Swift, Rust, Java, Kotlin, Scala, C#, Ruby, and PHP codebases, on macOS, Linux, or Windows.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_93cd3ae6d87b222eb6a4a51d3efd2191dcf7c5d0e0ea12d668a01d500e1e1223","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"kunal12203/graperoot@e21c5b9cd3e3 snapshot 657d207f0df5b456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9895f7562835c6096ff45519b5a4e8815f0016c005a3c076c82c8055c3dcc5b0","slc_bad431f1aa70fd333b92818aee3e8fbc1b1fd652e85656a474f1c3580bfc7083","slc_d91104f4a18b10fc087c6f136e6dea5eaa30dab95916707b2e349e9b32116dc5","slc_e75c8ec56a975b13a111959c7f175e8add18621d22a051f7bddda2145f7cbf35","slc_fa1f034d2fa8b94deb7f027fdc2845dbf12779fdf9c308d3c26a4f8e55381a49"],"source_ids":["src_14a4201a4405575187012b548764bceb"],"text":"The `graperoot` CLI supports an interactive picker, `--version`, `--update`, `--no-auto-update`, `--auto-update`, and `--no-telemetry`/`--telemetry` flags per the README usage sections.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_96b6e692a00eeb3497137124f1eed4769aa8d3ae5a973da78a60fb3251625030","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"kunal12203/graperoot@e21c5b9cd3e3 snapshot 657d207f0df5b456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_374360b09390e1bd56a1a2bf3b6b04287685ace85d1f18fd1ba6a279e46b0d94","slc_5034218196da616fb2aaef9406c3228c9ce3b6a4c7bfb5985763470e78655f0c"],"source_ids":["src_14a4201a4405575187012b548764bceb"],"text":"The AI assistant can call graph-aware MCP tools (`graph_read`, `graph_retrieve`, `graph_neighbors`) to explore further, and read budgets are hard-capped per turn via environment variables like DG_HARD_MAX_READ_CHARS (default 4000) and DG_TURN_READ_BUDGET_CHARS (default 18000).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a2465bfe59d6e087aba968d090d7b07ad72c731ccfc3520f2dc0f82e2ff1278b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"kunal12203/graperoot@e21c5b9cd3e3 snapshot 657d207f0df5b456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27f20133835f93202cb9d9ab143a4ceec60d361cc49b89f7380b845f470e8e85","slc_530aa2dfd5a43f223a4ae5ebe185f0ec47066eb9227b139b89ff633c91fbe730","slc_aa839f0395134411c03b525d6d836279c7d6ffa50aadc5e12c7cf11a2fd5345b","slc_f34f3bd91b592c6a846c1bc26f7c70c74b7d8364d0097f3b18fc3c5f8864e0f9"],"source_ids":["src_14a4201a4405575187012b548764bceb"],"text":"Project data lives in `<project>/.dual-graph/` (info_graph.json for the semantic graph, chat_action_graph.json for session memory, context-store.json for persistent decisions/tasks/facts), with a global install at `~/.dual-graph/`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_49db7485999146198717f9ae8021b87a"}
